From: pocket-debs
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: h264: Wait for the second field before outputting a pair
Description:
 A field pair is decoded with two requests that share one capture
 buffer: the first field is queued with V4L2_BUF_FLAG_M2M_HOLD_CAPTURE_BUF
 and the second field uses a sub-request. The picture handed to
 output_picture() is the first field, and only its request was waited
 for. When the request of the second field was still pending, which
 happens for the last pair at the end of the stream (drain), the capture
 buffer was pushed downstream while the driver was still writing the
 second field into it, and the lines of that field came out wrong from
 time to time.
 .
 Wait for the request of the second field instead. The pending requests
 are completed in queue order, so this also completes the request of the
 first field, and the capture buffer is dequeued with the second one.
Forwarded: no
License: LGPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched file)
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
---
diff --git a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c
index 6d7f09a..542b2a8 100644
--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech264dec.c
@@ -1136,6 +1136,16 @@ gst_v4l2_codec_h264_dec_output_picture (GstH264Decoder * decoder,
   GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (self, "Output picture %u",
       codec_picture->system_frame_number);
 
+  /* The first field of a pair holds the capture buffer, the picture is only
+   * complete once the request of the second field is done. */
+  if (!picture->second_field && picture->other_field) {
+    GstV4l2Request *second_request =
+        gst_h264_picture_get_user_data (picture->other_field);
+
+    if (second_request)
+      request = second_request;
+  }
+
   ret = gst_v4l2_request_set_done (request);
   if (ret == 0) {
     GST_ELEMENT_ERROR (self, STREAM, DECODE,
